# Nuclear Directory

> A directory of the organizations and facilities in the US nuclear industry, and the agreements between them. Each fact links to the public document it came from.

## What it covers

- <%= number_with_delimiter(companies) %> companies: reactor developers, fuel and materials, components, waste and decommissioning, power plant owners and operators, power buyers, services, investors, and government and research.
- <%= number_with_delimiter(plants) %> plants and sites: power plants, test reactors, fuel plants and mines, with their units, owners and operators.
- Relationships between them, stated with fixed verbs: supplies, invests in, offtakes from, owns, operates, vendor for, subsidiary of.

## How facts are sourced

- Every fact on a page carries a numbered source link to the public document it came from, such as an NRC, DOE or EIA record, an SEC filing or a company release.
- A fact with no public source is not published.
- Each page shows when it was last checked.

## Main pages

- [All companies](<%= companies_url %>): the full list, with filters for technology and state.
<% categories.each do |category| -%>
- [<%= category.name %>](<%= companies_url(category: category.to_param) %>)
<% end -%>
- [Sitemap](<%= sitemap_url %>): every company and plant page.
- Company pages are at <%= companies_url %>/{slug}, plant pages at <%= root_url.chomp("/") %>/plants/{slug}.
- [Our crawler](<%= bot_url %>): how the directory collects its sources.
- [Disclaimer](<%= disclaimer_url %>) and [privacy](<%= privacy_url %>).

## Data and feeds

- [Open dataset](<%= data_url %>): every published company, plant and link, with their sources, as CSV and JSON, under CC BY 4.0. Archived on Zenodo: https://doi.org/<%= StructuredDataHelper::DATASET_DOI %>
- [What's new](<%= updates_feed_url %>): an Atom feed of newly approved facts, deals and news, each with its page and source.
- [Snapshot](<%= api_snapshot_url %>): a JSON summary of the directory's counts.
- Company and plant pages carry schema.org JSON-LD (Organization, Place) with their sources.

## Citing

- Link the page and name the source it lists. The numbered Sources section at the foot of each page gives the title, the publisher and the link of every source.
- Counts and dates change as records are added, so cite the page rather than a number.
- For the data as a whole, cite the dataset: Nuclear Directory (2026), US nuclear supply chain dataset, https://doi.org/<%= StructuredDataHelper::DATASET_DOI %>

## Crawling

- Search engines and AI crawlers are welcome; see [robots.txt](<%= robots_url %>). <%= SitemapsController::DISALLOWED.to_sentence %> are not for crawling.

## Corrections

- Each page has a "Report a correction" link. Or write to <%= DirectoryHelper::CORRECTIONS_EMAIL %>.
